From 9f1c4d2a7b3e4f5061728394a5b6c7d8e9f0a1b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 21:05:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH panvk-g610 001] panvk/csf: keep the fused tess gen pass opt-in

csf-v11/213 and csf-v11/219 let one workgroup run COUNT, the prefix sum
and (for small direct draws) the WITH_COUNTS tessellation itself. 219
gated that gen variant on its stack: quads need 5648 B of TLS and fall
back to panlib_tess_gen(), triangles need 3616 B and stayed fused.

On a Mali-G610 MC4 (gpu_id 0xa8670000, v10 CSF) the fused triangle
variant writes broken interior domain points.  PanProbe
tests/dxvk/vulkan/tessellation on this build: the two triangle-domain
cases draw only the three corner triangles of the patch
(tri_equal_l3 and winding_ccw_cull_back: 352 px where the patch covers
1128; every quad, isoline, point, indirect and GS case passes), and
tests/dxvk/vulkan/xfb tes_capture (triangles, level 1) ends the CSG with
status 0x050002c1 "exception 0xc1", an MMU translation fault, then the
subqueues time out and vkWaitForFences returns VK_TIMEOUT.

That is the same failure shape csf-v11/219 documented for quads on
G615 ("interior points come from the dynamically indexed tessellator
arrays, which live on the stack"), so the gate moves the triangle
variant to the path every quad already takes and that passes on this
device: panlib_tess_gen(), a separate many-workgroup dispatch after the
fused count/scan.

PANVK_TESS_FUSE_GEN_MAX now defaults to 0.  Setting it to 64 (or any
patch count) restores the fused gen pass on parts where it is
validated; PANVK_TESS_FUSE=0 still disables the fused count/scan too.

Tested GPU: none yet (Mali-G610 MC4 report only)
Mesa base range: 5a07217f034b3e50d8c7c7794f97a2df1742613b
Dependencies: csf-v11 + jm-v9 + jm-v7 (after them, before panvk-g610)
Validation test: PanProbe tessellation TESSELLATION_FAILS=0 and xfb
 all cases PASS on Mali-G610

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c
index e25566e..c6be671 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c
@@ -698,8 +698,17 @@ panvk_per_arch(create_device)(struct panvk_physical_device *physical_device,
       device->vk.enabled_features.tessellationShader;
    simple_mtx_init(&device->gpu_prerast_lock, mtx_plain);
    device->tess_opt.fuse = debug_get_num_option("PANVK_TESS_FUSE", 1) != 0;
+   /* csf-v11 tess-fuse-stack: the fused workgroup runs the WITH_COUNTS pass
+    * itself (the gen variant) only while a draw the CPU knows to have at most
+    * this many patches.  Opt-in: on a Mali-G610 MC4 the triangle variant
+    * (3616 B of TLS) writes broken interior domain points - PanProbe draws 3
+    * of the 9 triangles of an L3 triangle patch, and xfb tes_capture ends the
+    * CSG with exception 0xc1 (MMU fault).  Quads already fall back to
+    * panlib_tess_gen() on every part (5648 B), which passes there.
+    * PANVK_TESS_FUSE_GEN_MAX=64 restores the fused gen on validated parts.
+    */
    device->tess_opt.fuse_gen_max =
-      debug_get_num_option("PANVK_TESS_FUSE_GEN_MAX", 64);
+      debug_get_num_option("PANVK_TESS_FUSE_GEN_MAX", 0);
    device->tess_opt.setup_in_step =
       debug_get_num_option("PANVK_TESS_SETUP_STEP", 1) != 0;
    device->tess_opt.arenas =
